at the last meeting what's the difference between a free cut

00:28:58.965 --> 00:29:00.965
and a subdivision application.

00:29:03.765 --> 00:29:08.485
And so there's two things that come into play here. Our town

00:29:08.550 --> 00:29:10.870
adopted our subdivision regulations

00:29:10.870 --> 00:29:13.190
on 05/10/1956.

00:29:16.070 --> 00:29:17.110
So if

00:29:17.190 --> 00:29:19.270
a lot was divided prior to that,

00:29:21.475 --> 00:29:24.035
they're not part of any subdivision regulation

00:29:24.035 --> 00:29:25.795
and can go about their business.

00:29:26.675 --> 00:29:27.555
If they

00:29:28.755 --> 00:29:30.675
divide after that date,

00:29:30.835 --> 00:29:31.395
they

00:29:32.755 --> 00:29:33.555
have to

00:29:33.875 --> 00:29:37.430
abide by the subdivision regulations going forward.

00:29:38.550 --> 00:29:43.510
And as presently defined, the subdivision means that we're going to break a piece of property

00:29:43.750 --> 00:29:45.270
into three lots

00:29:45.510 --> 00:29:46.230
or more.

00:29:51.095 --> 00:29:56.455
Anyhow, those are the two the date and the number three. So let's say we had

00:29:57.095 --> 00:29:58.775
a piece of property here

00:29:59.520 --> 00:30:03.840
and we broke it into two as shown on the screen here and we did that

00:30:04.160 --> 00:30:05.120
prior to

00:30:05.680 --> 00:30:06.960
the 1956

00:30:06.960 --> 00:30:07.680
date.

00:30:09.760 --> 00:30:16.305
Each of these landowners for each of these pieces of property would then be able to go through and get a free cut

00:30:17.425 --> 00:30:20.065
if they wanted to further divide that property.

00:30:21.345 --> 00:30:22.945
And what that means is,

00:30:25.425 --> 00:30:32.860
since it's not, they're not dividing the land into more than three pieces, they don't have to comply with all the subdivision regulations.

00:30:36.300 --> 00:30:36.860
Now,

00:30:37.580 --> 00:30:39.340
somebody divided and took,

00:30:40.555 --> 00:30:44.395
broke this property into two after the subdivision regulations

00:30:44.395 --> 00:30:45.675
went into effect,

00:30:46.075 --> 00:30:50.075
and then either one of the property owners wants to go and divide it again,

00:30:50.875 --> 00:30:53.835
the property has already been divided into two.

00:30:54.315 --> 00:30:56.130
So the next division,

00:30:56.290 --> 00:30:57.090
even though

00:30:57.650 --> 00:30:59.490
property on the right

00:31:01.170 --> 00:31:02.930
and you divide it into,

00:31:03.890 --> 00:31:07.250
that's making three pieces of property out of the original

00:31:07.915 --> 00:31:11.115
section that was in effect when the subdivision

00:31:11.115 --> 00:31:12.555
rules went into effect.

00:31:12.875 --> 00:31:16.795
And so then you have to abide by all the subdivision regulations.

00:31:17.675 --> 00:31:18.875
That's the difference.

00:31:19.435 --> 00:31:20.715
If you don't

00:31:20.955 --> 00:31:23.995
have a subdivision, you have to

00:31:23.570 --> 00:31:25.890
